01:09:28.690 --> 01:09:32.390
If it's difficult to infer
causal relationships from data,

01:09:32.390 --> 01:09:35.756
as for example, the global
warming hiatus example,

01:09:35.756 --> 01:09:39.240
then it's difficult to
infer causal relationships

01:09:39.240 --> 01:09:42.160
from climate data of the past 100 years.

01:09:42.160 --> 01:09:44.910
The last 100 years is a blip
compared to the millions

01:09:44.910 --> 01:09:46.930
of years of climate data.

01:09:46.930 --> 01:09:51.230
As climate warming skeptics
argue that our blips over many

01:09:51.230 --> 01:09:53.550
years in which the earth warms and cools,

01:09:53.550 --> 01:09:56.021
perhaps we find ourselves
in a warming blip,

01:09:56.021 --> 01:10:00.130
the reply to this line
stresses that we shouldn't rely

01:10:00.130 --> 01:10:02.610
on the data, but our causal knowledge

01:10:02.610 --> 01:10:05.023
of the role of CO2 in the atmosphere.

01:10:06.480 --> 01:10:09.730
Yet, if that's the correct
response to the global warming

01:10:09.730 --> 01:10:12.530
skeptic, then it seems
a defense of masking

01:10:12.530 --> 01:10:17.150
and social distancing
can rely on our knowledge

